Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||05-23-2001||10:23 AM||||Hey guys and gals, I've been hearing this hum from the back end of the car for a few days, new tires and alignment didn't fix it up, and it sounds to be MPH related. I searched the archives to see if it could be the bearings, but I'm not getting any symptoms like the ones I found described. it's pretty consistant, and pretty quiet, it doesn't change in the corners, just sounds kinda like road noise, but I know it wasn't there before. And with the fierostore charging $90 for rear bearings, I don't want to just take a guess. anyone ever have these symptoms before?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wade87GT||05-23-2001||11:52 AM||||My guess would be tread noise from the new tires. Different tread designs produce different sounds.||||reg||3
Z||000002||stsmithgt||05-23-2001||12:33 PM||||The last set of tires I had sounded like a UFO landing when I'd slow coming off the freeway.  A real creepy sound.  Check your fluid levels in your tranny.  Hopfully you don't have a grumbling hum.  I had to change a hub to get rid of a noise like that.(250 for the part and 250 to get it put in.) I wish I had a garage and a second car so I'd have time to work on it myself, but it's too expensive here to rent a place with a garage unless I get a roomate. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
